This directory contains code derived from scCRAFT:

  He, C., Filippidis, P., Kleinstein, S.H., Guan, L. (2025).
  "Partially characterized topology guides reliable anchor-free scRNA-integration."
  Commun. Biol. 8(1):561.
  Source: https://github.com/ch2343/scCRAFT

The VAE backbone (Encoder/Decoder/VAE), the negative-binomial likelihood
(log_nb_positive), the Gaussian reparameterization, the triplet loss and
multi-resolution clustering (utils.py), and CrossEntropy are upstream scCRAFT,
with local modifications by K. Reid (warmup flag, raw-counts NB path, batch-effect
decoder pathway). Retained under scCRAFT's original license.

Everything under the sibling wcd/ package (reference Wasserstein critic, adversarial
head dispatch, alternative VAE backbones, adversarial training engine, LISI/evaluation
metrics, data preprocessing, and the nested-CV / Pareto experiment harness) is the
authored contribution of this work and is NOT part of upstream scCRAFT.
